{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4521","id":4733925932,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGin6LA","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4521","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4521.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4521.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4521","number":4521,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A00-T07.6: reject stale claim operations after lease replacement","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A00-T07.6\nRefs #1083. Regression fix to the completed claim implementation; this does not reopen the leaf or claim live Project qualification.\n\n## Problem and resulting behavior\n\nA claim can be released and replaced between an operation's initial read and its mutex creation. The old operation previously reloaded the replacement claim and could reconcile it away, including a new owner's locks. This change binds the operation to the inspected generation, reloads after acquiring the mutex, and rejects changed task identity, missing claims or replacement generations before making ownership mutations.\n\nThe existing exclusive-operation seam protects reconciliation, ordinary release, heartbeat, lock/unlock and reaping. Same-generation heartbeats remain valid: the operation uses the current sequence and expiry rather than requiring an unchanged commit SHA. A stale reaper stops and must be retried from a fresh snapshot. Existing owner, expiry, reason and mutex checks remain intact.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Parent `ca3c083b`: the 10 new deterministic race tests produced 9 failures and 1 passing same-generation control.\n- Candidate local commit `d2504f7d`, tree `23b492442a99984263b09f3b924a9b4343baa528`: 28/28 focused and existing claim tests passed, with no skips.\n- `npm run check` passed with 3,691 linked modules, and `npm run build` passed. `npm run check:structure` exited 0 with the repository's existing advisory violations; no changed file added a reported violation.\n- Node 24.19.0, npm 11.9.0, Linux x64. Tests executed serially through `node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap planning/contracts/tests/claim-generation-race.test.js planning/contracts/tests/claim-race.test.js`.\n\nPublication used the GitHub connector and verified the remote tree equals the tested tree. The connector assigns commit metadata, so the published SHA differs from the local validation commit. Required hosted core at the published head remains the merge gate.\n\n## Scope and coordination\n\nTwo files only. No production runtime changes, new dependencies, live claim/lock/ref reconciliation, Project field updates, or provider operations are included. All race tests use the existing fake GitHub transport; they do not assert production-service qualification. No active lease is asserted by this new regression branch.","created_at":"2026-10-04T11:21:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T11:25:19Z",